--- /dev/null
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Files that belong to this repository's own development loop and not to the package a consumer
+# depends on. `export-ignore` keeps them out of `git archive` output, which is what GitHub's source
+# tarballs and `swift package archive-source` are built from. It cannot keep them out of a `git
+# clone`, and nothing can: a consumer who clones the repository gets the repository.
+PLAN.md export-ignore
+BACKLOG.md export-ignore
+JOURNAL.md export-ignore
+JOURNAL-archive.md export-ignore
+.jeffy export-ignore
